@event know_kael_thaw
# en: Before the Break
title [60004e] = 放假之前
# en: The last barge before the winter break is loading, and Kael is at the landing with his trunk, not quite looking at you. He's been strange all week. Back home, he told you once, saying goodbye is bad luck. The barge horn sounds. He's waiting, as if there were something you might say.
text [e113f2] = 寒假前的最后一班驳船正在装货，凯尔带着行李箱站在码头上，不太看你。他这一星期都怪怪的。他跟你说过，在他老家，说再见是不吉利的。驳船的汽笛响了。他在等，好像你也许会说点什么。
# en: A barge landing in the snow at the end of term, students with trunks waiting to leave, two of them standing face to face at the edge of the jetty.
scene [923204] = 学期末雪中的驳船码头，学生们带着行李等着离开，其中两人在栈桥边上面对面站着。
# en: Shake his hand
opt.left.label [e76d26] = 和他握手
# en: You shake his hand, and wish him a good break. He says "and you", and climbs aboard, and doesn't look back. You realise, as the barge rounds the bend, that he was waiting for something else.
opt.left.say.1 [6f20ed] = 你和他握了握手，祝他假期愉快。他说“你也是”，爬上了船，没有回头。驳船绕过河弯时你才意识到，他等的是别的东西。
# en: "Until the thaw."
opt.right.label [23517c] = “冰融时见。”
# en: "Until the thaw," you say, and touch your forehead to his. He goes very still. Then he laughs, a short surprised breath, and says it back, so the cold knows you're coming back. He waves from the barge all the way round the bend.
opt.right.say.1 [af7bd8] = “冰融时见，”你说，把额头抵在他的额头上。他一下子僵住了。然后他笑了，短短地、惊讶地吐了口气，也对你说了这句话，好让寒冷知道你们还会回来。驳船绕过河弯之前，他一直在挥手。

@event know_ilse_useless
# en: Ilse, Losing
title [a863da] = 伊尔泽输了
# en: Ilse's frost-work has gone wrong for the first time anyone has seen. She's sitting on the frozen pond beside a sculpture that has cracked down the middle, and the private snowstorm over her head has turned to sleet. "Go away," she says. "Or teach me something. I don't care which."
text [d92fac] = 伊尔泽的冰霜作品头一回在众人眼前出了岔子。她独自坐在结冰的池塘上，身旁一座冰雕从中间裂开了，头顶那场私人暴风雪变成了冻雨。“走开，”她说，“要么教我点什么。哪样都行。”
# en: A frozen pond at dusk, a girl in white furs sitting alone on the ice with a ruined frost-sculpture beside her, snow falling only on her.
scene [7c8d9f] = 黄昏结冰的池塘上，一个裹着白色毛皮的女孩独自坐着，身旁是一座毁掉的冰雕，雪只落在她一个人身上。
# en: Help her mend the sculpture
opt.left.label [f184b7] = 帮她修补冰雕
# en: You hold the crack while she seals it, and it takes, and the sculpture stands. She looks at it critically. "Useful," she says, as if that were an insult. The sleet eases, a little.
opt.left.say.1 [7c3675] = 你扶住裂缝，她把它封上，封住了，冰雕立了起来。她挑剔地看着它。“有用，”她说，像是在骂人。冻雨稍微小了一点。
# en: You make it worse. The sculpture falls in two. Ilse looks at the pieces, then at you. "Well," she says. "Now we're both bad at it." It isn't quite a joke.
opt.left.say.2 [f2415f] = 你越弄越糟。冰雕裂成了两半。伊尔泽看看碎块，又看看你。“好吧，”她说，“现在我们俩都不行了。”这不太算是个玩笑。
# en: Teach her to skim stones across the ice
opt.right.label [f27895] = 教她在冰上打水漂
# en: You teach her something completely useless: skimming stones across the ice, as far as they'll go. She counts every bounce out loud, in Northern. The sleet turns back to snow. When you leave, she's still at it, alone, counting, and very nearly smiling.
opt.right.say.1 [04ff9a] = 你教她一件毫无用处的事：让石子在冰面上跳着滑出去，越远越好。每跳一下她都用北地话大声数出来。冻雨又变回了雪。你离开时她还在那儿，一个人，数着，几乎在笑。

@event know_ilse_stitch
# en: A Torn Ward
title [aec809] = 撕破的护符
# en: You find a frost-ward charm in the snow by the courtyard fountain, torn half through, the kind Ilse makes. Without it, whoever lost it will feel the cold all winter. The stitching is unusual, a looping Northern pattern. You have a needle and some silver thread.
text [4f5032] = 你在庭院喷泉边的雪里捡到一个冰霜护符，撕破了一半，是伊尔泽做的那种。没了它，丢东西的人一整个冬天都会觉得冷。针脚很特别，是一种绕圈的北地针法。你身上正好有一根针和一些银线。
# en: A courtyard bench in winter, a torn white frost-ward charm lying in a student's hands, a needle and silver thread beside it.
scene [b895e3] = 冬天庭院的长凳上，一个撕破的白色冰霜护符躺在一个学生手里，旁边放着针和银线。
# en: Take it to the lost-property box
opt.left.label [1b78a2] = 交到失物招领箱
# en: You hand it in. Somebody claims it the next day: a second-year who has been shivering for a week. Ilse, you hear later, made her a new one, without being asked, and without saying anything.
opt.left.say.1 [5bd2cf] = 你把它交了上去。第二天就有人认领了：一个已经冻得发抖一个星期的二年级生。你后来听说，伊尔泽给她做了个新的，没人请她，她也什么都没说。
# en: Mend it with her mother's stitch
opt.right.label [b4f66b] = 用她母亲的针法补好
# en: You mend it slowly, in the looping stitch, the one that was her mother's. When you hand it to Ilse, she turns it over, finds the mend, and goes very quiet. Kael, beside her, touches it once. "Mother's," he says. Neither of them says anything else, for a long time.
opt.right.say.1 [887280] = 你用那种绕圈的针法慢慢地补，那是她母亲的针法。你把它交给伊尔泽时，她翻过来，找到了补过的地方，一下子安静了。她身边的凯尔摸了一下。“是母亲的，”他说。很长一段时间，他们俩谁都没再说话。

@event know_isolde_chess
# en: Called to the Tower
title [f0d27f] = 被叫到塔上
# en: You've been sent to the headmistress over a complaint from a lecturer: a broken window, a misunderstanding, a lot of shouting. Headmistress Marrow reads the letter, then looks at you over it. Behind her, the tower chess game by the window is half finished, and one of her towers is in trouble.
text [34c356] = 一位讲师投诉了你，你被送到了院长那里：一扇打碎的窗，一场误会，一通大喊大叫。马罗院长读完信，从信纸上方看着你。她身后，窗边的塔棋下到一半，她的一座塔有麻烦了。
# en: A tall tower study, a chessboard of crystal towers by the window mid-game, a headmistress behind a desk with a letter of complaint open in front of her.
scene [981aaa] = 高高的塔楼书房，窗边一盘下到一半的水晶塔棋，院长坐在书桌后，面前摊着一封投诉信。
# en: Explain, very carefully
opt.left.label [da77bf] = 非常小心地解释
# en: You explain, carefully and truthfully, and she listens without interrupting. At the end she folds the letter. "Pay for the glass," she says. "And apologise properly." It could have gone a great deal worse.
opt.left.say.1 [5a065a] = 你小心而如实地解释了，她听着，没有打断。最后她把信折了起来。“赔玻璃，”她说，“好好道个歉。”本来可能糟糕得多。
# en: You explain, and it comes out sounding like an excuse even to you. She hears you out, and fines you for the window, and makes you write the apology twice.
opt.left.say.2 [6bff15] = 你解释了，可连你自己听着都像借口。她听你说完，罚你赔窗户，还让你把道歉信写了两遍。
# en: Offer to finish her game
opt.right.label [8d2ae4] = 提出替她下完这盘棋
# en: "Your tower's in trouble," you say. She looks at you, and then at the board, and says "Is it?" You play it out together. She loses, and laughs, short and delighted. Then she folds the letter. "Pay for the glass," she says. "Come back and lose to me properly, sometime."
opt.right.say.1 [81aaaa] = “您的塔有麻烦了，”你说。她看看你，又看看棋盘，说：“是吗？”你们一起下完了。她输了，短促而高兴地笑了一声。然后她把信折了起来。“赔玻璃，”她说，“改天再来，好好输给我一回。”

@event know_nessa_off_record
# en: Asking About a Friend
title [69bed0] = 打听一位朋友
# en: Nessa wants to ask you about a friend of yours, who's in trouble with the prefects and who you'd rather nobody wrote about. "I'll print it either way," she says. "I'd rather print it right." Her quill is already moving, taking down everything you say, including your sighs.
text [03b52e] = 内莎想问你一位朋友的事，对方和级长们闹了麻烦，你宁愿谁也别写这件事。“不管怎样我都会登，”她说，“我宁可登得准确。”她的羽毛笔已经在动了，把你说的一切都记了下来，包括你的叹气。
# en: A newspaper office, an editor at her desk, a self-writing quill poised over a notebook, a student in the visitor's chair with arms folded.
scene [5a27a1] = 报社办公室里，一位编辑坐在桌边，一支自动羽毛笔悬在笔记本上方，来访者椅子上的学生抱着胳膊。
# en: Give her the friendly version
opt.left.label [de53f7] = 给她一个友善的版本
# en: You give her the kindest true version you can, and the quill takes it down. The piece runs, fair and short. Your friend is grateful, mostly. The quill added an adjective you didn't say.
opt.left.say.1 [b304fb] = 你给了她你能给的最友善的真实版本，羽毛笔记了下来。报道登了，公道而简短。你的朋友大体上很感激。羽毛笔多加了一个你没说过的形容词。
# en: "This is off the record."
opt.right.label [045e5e] = “这是不对外的。”
# en: "Off the record," you say, and the quill stops mid-word and lies down on the desk. Nessa looks at it, and at you, and something in her face changes. You tell her the whole of it. She never prints a line, and the next week she helps your friend with the prefects instead.
opt.right.say.1 [d50fc7] = “不对外，”你说，羽毛笔在一个字写到一半时停了下来，躺倒在桌上。内莎看看它，又看看你，脸上有什么变了。你把整件事都告诉了她。她一行字都没登，下个星期还去帮你的朋友应付了级长。

@event know_nessa_planted
# en: The Proofs
title [b816b3] = 校样
# en: Nessa drops a stack of proofs on the desk in front of you and goes to make tea, very casually. "Errors," she says from the doorway. "Find them before the printers come. There might be one." There are, you can see already, at least four.
text [1ee516] = 内莎把一摞校样扔在你面前的桌上，若无其事地去泡茶了。“错误，”她在门口说，“印刷工来之前找出来。也许有一个。”你一眼就看出来，至少有四个。
# en: A cluttered newspaper office at night, galley proofs spread over a desk under a lamp, an editor watching a student from across the room.
scene [50060f] = 入夜后杂乱的报社办公室，灯下的桌上摊着长条校样，一位编辑从房间那头看着一个学生。
# en: Fix everything you can find
opt.left.label [26b85f] = 能找到的都改掉
# en: You find four errors and fix them, and a fifth that turns out to be the editor's style. Nessa reads your corrections, nods, and points to a sixth, in the headline, that you missed. "Close," she says.
opt.left.say.1 [99755d] = 你找到了四个错误改掉了，还有第五个，结果是编辑的文风。内莎读了你的修改，点点头，指出了第六个，在标题里，你漏了。“差一点，”她说。
# en: Find hers first
opt.right.label [5e8da4] = 先找她埋的那个
# en: You find the planted one first: a date that couldn't be true, set in the middle of the page like a trap. You circle it, and only then fix the others. Nessa comes back with the tea, sees the circle, and laughs out loud. "Nobody's ever gone for that one first," she says. "You're hired. Unpaid, obviously."
opt.right.say.1 [db5c10] = 你先找到了她埋的那个：一个不可能对的日期，像陷阱一样摆在版面中间。你把它圈了出来，然后才去改别的。内莎端着茶回来，看见那个圈，大笑出声。“从没人先去找那个，”她说，“你被录用了。没有工钱，当然。”
# en: You hunt for whichever error she meant, and can't tell which it is, and run out of time before the printers come. Nessa takes the proofs back with a small, satisfied smile. "There's always one," she says, and doesn't say which. The hunt, you have to admit, was fun.
opt.right.say.2 [3a3090] = 你到处找她说的是哪个错误，分辨不出来，印刷工来之前就没时间了。内莎带着一丝得意的微笑把校样收了回去。“总会有一个的，”她说，却没说是哪个。你得承认，找的过程挺有意思。

@event know_seraphine_too_loud
# en: Lost at Lantern Night
title [65fdca] = 灯笼夜走失
# en: Lantern Night, and the whole academy and half the village are on the lakeshore, laughing, singing, all their futures at once. Somebody says Seraphine was here a minute ago and now she isn't. Her friends are searching the crowd, calling her name over the music.
text [25f04e] = 灯笼夜，整个学院和半个村子都在湖岸上，笑着，唱着，所有人的未来一齐涌来。有人说塞拉芬刚才还在这儿，现在不见了。她的朋友们在人群里找，压过音乐喊着她的名字。
# en: A crowded lakeshore at night strung with floating lanterns, a press of students and villagers, one dark boathouse at the edge with its door ajar.
scene [c92fb1] = 夜里挂满浮灯的湖岸挤满了学生和村民，岸边尽头一间黑黢黢的船屋，门半开着。
# en: Search the crowd with them
opt.left.label [48ac21] = 和他们一起在人群里找
# en: You push through the crowd for an hour, calling her name. Someone finds her in the end, sitting very still in the dark of the boathouse, and she says she's fine, and isn't, and goes back to bed early.
opt.left.say.1 [2a40c7] = 你在人群里挤了一个小时，喊着她的名字。最后有人在船屋的黑暗里找到了她，她一动不动地坐着，说她没事，其实有事，早早回去睡了。
# en: Look for her somewhere dark
opt.right.label [d6e0c7] = 去黑暗的地方找她
# en: You don't look in the crowd. You walk away from it, to the dark boathouse at the end, and she's there on an upturned boat with her eyes shut. You sit down beside her without a word. After a while she says, "Quiet." Then: "Yours." You stay till the lanterns are all out.
opt.right.say.1 [eeac21] = 你没在人群里找。你离开人群，走向尽头黑黢黢的船屋，她就在那儿，坐在一只翻扣的船上，闭着眼睛。你一言不发地在她身边坐下。过了一会儿她说：“安静。”然后：“你的。”你一直待到灯笼全都熄灭。

@event know_thorne_hands
# en: The Demonstration
title [6b9817] = 示范
# en: Thorne is demonstrating a duelling stance to the whole year, wand raised, and halfway through the demonstration his wand hand begins to shake. It's small. Most of the hall hasn't noticed yet. He has. You can see him deciding whether to stop.
text [ea2ef6] = 索恩正在给整个年级示范一个决斗架势，魔杖举着，示范到一半，他握杖的手开始发抖。很轻微。大厅里大多数人还没注意到。他注意到了。你看得出他在决定要不要停下来。
# en: A lecture hall, an old professor at the front with his wand raised for a demonstration, its tip trembling very slightly, a student in the front row rising from their seat.
scene [2c6a85] = 阶梯教室里，一位老教授站在前面举着魔杖示范，杖尖微微颤抖，第一排一个学生正从座位上站起来。
# en: Look away, and let him finish
opt.left.label [9f4249] = 移开目光，让他示范完
# en: You look down at your notes, and so, after a moment, does the rest of the front row. Thorne finishes the demonstration with his other hand, briskly, and dismisses the class early. You're fairly sure that was the right thing.
opt.left.say.1 [ef5468] = 你低头看笔记，过了一会儿，第一排其他人也跟着低下了头。索恩换了一只手，利落地示范完，提前下了课。你很确定这样做是对的。
# en: Ask to be his demonstration partner
opt.right.label [3bc361] = 请求当他的示范搭档
# en: "Could you show it on someone, sir?" you ask, and step up before he can answer. He takes your wrist instead of his wand, and shows the stance with your arm, steady, the whole year watching. Afterwards he says, "Hm." It's the warmest thing he's ever said to you.
opt.right.say.1 [f22b54] = “先生，能在人身上示范一下吗？”你问，不等他回答就走了上去。他没拿魔杖，而是握住你的手腕，用你的胳膊示范那个架势，稳稳的，全年级都看着。之后他说：“嗯。”这是他对你说过的最温暖的话。

@event know_tamsin_failed
# en: Exam Nerves, by Post
title [4ae610] = 邮寄来的考前紧张
# en: Tamsin's letter is short again. They're sitting their advanced illusion examination next week, and they can't sleep, and every insult in the letter is half-hearted, which is how you know. "Say something," the postscript says. "Anything. I'm not asking. Obviously."
text [5a73ae] = 塔姆辛的信又很短。TA下周要考高级幻术，睡不着觉，信里每一句挖苦都有气无力，你就是凭这个看出来的。“说点什么，”附言写道，“什么都行。我可没在求你。显然。”
# en: A letter on a dormitory desk, its handwriting cramped and blotted, a student holding a quill over a blank reply.
scene [e5cdca] = 宿舍书桌上放着一封信，字迹挤成一团，还有墨渍，一个学生拿着羽毛笔，对着一张空白的回信。
# en: Send them luck and a sketch
opt.left.label [727f5e] = 寄去好运和一幅速写
# en: You send a sketch of a goat in a mortarboard, labelled "your examiner", and a great deal of luck. Their reply comes a fortnight later: "Passed. The goat helped. Insufferable of you."
opt.left.say.1 [151e76] = 你寄去了一幅戴学位帽的山羊速写，标注“你的考官”，还有满满的好运。两个星期后TA回了信：“过了。山羊帮了忙。你真讨厌。”
# en: Remind them of the last time
opt.right.label [7967f5] = 提醒TA上一次的事
# en: You write about the last time: the failed exam, the sold theatre, the retake, and how they passed it anyway with everything gone. "You've done harder," you write. Their reply comes the day after the exam, one line: "You remembered. Top marks. I cried in the refectory again."
opt.right.say.1 [f3d4ef] = 你写了上一次的事：那场失利的考试，卖掉的剧团，补考，以及TA在一无所有的时候照样考过了。“你经历过更难的，”你写道。TA的回信在考试第二天到了，只有一行：“你记得。最高分。我又在膳堂里哭了。”
# en: You write that they'll be fine, and that you're sure they've done harder things. Their reply is cheerful and vague. They passed, but they don't say much else, and you have the feeling you missed something.
opt.right.say.2 [51ac9d] = 你写道TA会没事的，你相信TA经历过更难的事。TA的回信轻松而含糊。TA考过了，却没多说什么，你隐约觉得自己错过了什么。

@event know_grimsby_nose
# en: The Night Before the Essay
title [c699b5] = 交论文的前一晚
# en: Your essay is due tomorrow, and the one book you need isn't in the library. You reach Grimsby's as he's turning the sign to "closed". He lets you in, holds up the lamp to a wall of a thousand spines, and says, "Well? What does it look like?"
text [2502ec] = 你的论文明天就要交，而你需要的那本书图书馆里没有。你赶到格林斯比书店时，他正把牌子翻到“打烊”。他让你进来，举着灯照向一整面墙上千本书脊，说：“说吧？它长什么样？”
# en: A village bookshop at closing time, a student at the counter out of breath, the bookseller holding a lamp up to a wall of shelves.
scene [b7c026] = 打烊时分的村里书店，一个学生气喘吁吁地站在柜台前，书商把一盏灯举向一整面书架。
# en: Describe the title and the author
opt.left.label [b313c2] = 说出书名和作者
# en: You tell him the title and the author. He brightens and goes off into the shelves, and comes back an hour later with a book about lighthouses, and then, at last, the right one, as the clock in the square strikes ten.
opt.left.say.1 [051b19] = 你告诉他书名和作者。他眼睛一亮，钻进书架里，一个小时后先拿回来一本关于灯塔的书，然后，终于，拿来了对的那本，这时广场上的钟敲了十下。
# en: Describe how it smells
opt.right.label [6981b9] = 描述它的气味
# en: "Old paper and rain," you say, "and something like cloves." Grimsby's face lights up. He closes his eyes, takes three steps, and pulls it off the shelf without looking. "Nobody ever asks properly," he says, and won't take your money.
opt.right.say.1 [747160] = “旧纸和雨水，”你说，“还有点像丁香。”格林斯比的脸一下子亮了。他闭上眼睛，走了三步，看都不看就从书架上抽出了那本书。“从没人好好地问过，”他说，不肯收你的钱。

@event know_pell_counting
# en: The Good Stock
title [086c07] = 上等的存货
# en: You need a strong remedy for a friend with a fever, and Pell has the good stock, in a dark bottle on the top shelf he sells only to people he trusts. Everyone else gets the shop's ordinary tincture. Pell looks at you over his spectacles and starts to measure out the ordinary one.
text [777216] = 你需要一剂强效药给一个发烧的朋友，佩尔有上等的存货，装在最高一层架子上的一只深色瓶子里，只卖给他信得过的人。其他人拿到的是店里普通的酊剂。佩尔从眼镜上方看了看你，开始量那普通的。
# en: An apothecary's counter lined with brass scales and a wall of tiny drawers, an old man in spectacles measuring drops into a vial while a student watches.
scene [65ae1f] = 药铺柜台上摆着一排黄铜秤，背后是一面墙的小抽屉，一位戴眼镜的老人正往小瓶里滴药，一个学生在旁边看着。
# en: Go to the infirmary instead
opt.left.label [9b6746] = 改去医务室
# en: You thank him and take your friend to the infirmary instead, where Sister Amaranth's ordinary tonic works, slowly. Your friend is up in a week, and grateful, and you wonder whether the dark bottle would have done it in a day.
opt.left.say.1 [aa2748] = 你谢过他，带朋友去了医务室，阿玛兰斯修女普通的补药慢慢起了作用。你的朋友一个星期后就起来了，很感激你，而你在想，那只深色瓶子会不会一天就能治好。
# en: Count the drops aloud with him
opt.right.label [28b940] = 和他一起大声数滴数
# en: You count the drops aloud as he measures, quietly, one to nine. Pell stops at four and looks at you. Then he puts the ordinary bottle away and reaches for the top shelf. "Measure twice," he says, counting with you. Your friend is up the next morning.
opt.right.say.1 [29b854] = 他量的时候你小声数着，从一数到九。数到四时佩尔停了下来，看着你。然后他把普通的瓶子放回去，伸手去够最高一层。“量两遍，”他说，和你一起数着。第二天早上你的朋友就起来了。

@event know_amaranth_truth
# en: Patched Up
title [6b956d] = 包扎
# en: You come into the infirmary with an arm that's swelling fast, from something you'd rather not explain. Sister Amaranth turns it to the light and asks, as she always does, how it happened. Behind you there's a queue. Your story is ready: a fall on the stairs.
text [b31677] = 你走进医务室，一只胳膊肿得飞快，原因你不太想解释。阿玛兰斯修女把它转向光，像往常一样问你是怎么弄的。你身后排着队。你的说辞已经准备好了：在楼梯上摔了一跤。
# en: An infirmary bench, a student holding a bruised arm, a healer in a grey apron turning it to the light from the window.
scene [7f18a3] = 医务室的长凳上，一个学生捧着一只淤青的胳膊，一位系灰围裙的医师把它转向窗口的光。
# en: Tell her about the stairs
opt.left.label [507bd7] = 跟她说楼梯的事
# en: You tell her about the stairs. She listens, and waits, and treats it, slowly, with a salve that stings. "Come back in two days," she says. "Bring the truth with you next time. It heals faster."
opt.left.say.1 [77e374] = 你跟她说了楼梯的事。她听着，等着，然后慢慢地给你涂了一种刺痛的药膏。“两天后再来，”她说，“下次把实话带来。实话好得快。”
# en: Tell her the true version, first
opt.right.label [ddb70c] = 先告诉她真实的版本
# en: You skip the stairs and tell her exactly what happened, embarrassing as it is. She nods once. "Better," she says, and reaches for a bottle that isn't a salve. The swelling's gone before you reach the door.
opt.right.say.1 [724bdb] = 你跳过楼梯，原原本本地告诉她发生了什么，尽管很丢脸。她点了一下头。“这才对，”她说，伸手拿了一瓶不是药膏的东西。你还没走到门口，肿就消了。

@event know_marisol_spirits
# en: The Storm Crossing
title [9188db] = 风暴中渡湖
# en: You're halfway across the lake in a borrowed boat when the storm comes in, fast and black. The waves are full of shapes like galloping horses: the water spirits, racing the boat and, by the look of it, enjoying themselves. The shore is a long way off.
text [46bb4f] = 你划着一条借来的船到了湖中央，风暴来了，又快又黑。浪里满是像奔马一样的影子：是水灵，在和小船赛跑，看样子玩得很开心。岸还远着呢。
# en: A small boat on a choppy grey lake under a storm sky, a student at the oars, shapes like galloping horses moving in the waves around the boat.
scene [83893a] = 暴风雨的天空下，一条小船在灰色起伏的湖面上，一个学生握着桨，船周围的浪里有奔马一样的影子在跑。
# en: Row for it
opt.left.label [6a8d31] = 拼命划
# en: You row until your hands are raw, and the spirits race you all the way, and lose, just. You land on the shingle soaked to the skin, and lie there laughing at the sky.
opt.left.say.1 [a658f9] = 你划到手都磨破了，水灵一路和你赛跑，最后以毫厘之差输了。你浑身湿透地爬上卵石滩，躺在那里对着天空大笑。
# en: The spirits win. They tip the boat over, cheerfully, ten yards from shore, and you swim the rest in the cold. You arrive half drowned, and they gallop off, delighted with themselves.
opt.left.say.2 [641100] = 水灵赢了。它们兴高采烈地在离岸十码的地方把船掀翻了，你在冷水里游完了剩下的路。你上岸时半死不活，它们得意洋洋地跑开了。
# en: Ask them nicely not to cheat
opt.right.label [c54aa7] = 客客气气地请它们别作弊
# en: You ship the oars, lean over the side and ask the spirits, very politely, not to cheat. There's a pause. Then they gather under the boat like a raft and carry you to shore at a gallop. Marisol, on the steps with her book, laughs so hard she drops it.
opt.right.say.1 [46a9c5] = 你收起桨，探出船舷，非常礼貌地请水灵们不要作弊。安静了一下。然后它们聚在船底，像一只木筏一样驮着你一路奔向岸边。拿着书坐在台阶上的玛丽索尔笑得书都掉了。

@event know_vey_smell
# en: The Feast That Wasn't
title [cd1736] = 不存在的盛宴
# en: Some third-years have laid on a feast at the end of the long table: roast fowl, pies, a cake with candles. The whole table is reaching for it. It's beautiful. It's a little too beautiful. Somewhere at the far end, the third-years are trying very hard not to laugh.
text [5026c1] = 几个三年级生在长桌尽头摆了一桌盛宴：烤禽、馅饼、插着蜡烛的蛋糕。整张桌子的人都在伸手。它很美。美得有点过头了。远处那几个三年级生正拼命忍着不笑。
# en: A refectory table laden with a glorious feast, students reaching hungrily for it, one student pausing with a fork in mid-air and sniffing.
scene [e999fc] = 膳堂的长桌上摆满了丰盛的宴席，学生们饥肠辘辘地伸手去拿，一个学生举着叉子停在半空，嗅了嗅。
# en: Dig in with everyone
opt.left.label [625d2f] = 和大家一起开吃
# en: You reach for the pie with everyone else, and your fork goes through it and into the table, and the whole feast dissolves into air and a few crumbs of real bread. The third-years cheer. Everyone laughs, you included, eventually.
opt.left.say.1 [71e4c1] = 你和大家一起伸手去拿馅饼，叉子穿过馅饼戳到了桌子上，整桌宴席化作空气和几粒真面包屑。三年级生们欢呼起来。大家都笑了，你最后也笑了。
# en: Smell it first
opt.right.label [c9ea73] = 先闻一闻
# en: You lean in and sniff. Nothing: not roast, not pastry, not a crumb. "It doesn't smell of anything," you say, loudly. The table stops. The third-years groan. Somewhere, you feel, Professor Vey would be proud, and would never say so.
opt.right.say.1 [00f92e] = 你凑过去闻了闻。什么味道也没有：没有烤肉味，没有面点味，一点碎屑味都没有。“它什么味道都没有，”你大声说。整张桌子停了下来。三年级生们哀叹一声。你觉得，维伊教授要是在场会很骄傲，却绝不会说出口。

@event know_brask_asking
# en: Out of Your Depth
title [706966] = 力不从心
# en: Brask has handed you a lead rope and a griffin with opinions, and walked away to the fence. The griffin has decided it would like to be somewhere else, and it's bigger than you. Everyone else in the class seems to be managing. Brask is watching, arms folded, saying nothing.
text [c13d5d] = 布拉斯克把一根缰绳和一头很有主见的狮鹫交给你，然后走到了栅栏边。狮鹫打定主意想去别处，而且它比你大。班上其他人似乎都应付得来。布拉斯克抱着胳膊看着，一言不发。
# en: A stable yard, a large and irritable griffin pulling against a rope held by a nervous student, a professor in a leather apron watching from the fence.
scene [98467c] = 马厩的院子里，一头暴躁的大狮鹫拽着一个紧张的学生手里的缰绳，一位系皮围裙的教授在栅栏边看着。
# en: Manage it yourself
opt.left.label [624184] = 自己搞定
# en: You dig your heels in and talk to it in a low voice, the way Brask talks to everything but students, and slowly the griffin comes round. Brask nods, once. From her that's a medal.
opt.left.say.1 [b40eb7] = 你蹬住脚跟，用低沉的声音跟它说话，就像布拉斯克跟除了学生以外的一切说话那样，狮鹫慢慢平静了下来。布拉斯克点了一下头。从她那里得到这个，就是一枚勋章。
# en: The griffin wins. It drags you halfway across the yard and into a water trough before Brask takes the rope from your hand with two fingers. "Hm," she says. "Again tomorrow."
opt.left.say.2 [9d390a] = 狮鹫赢了。它把你拖过半个院子，拖进了水槽，布拉斯克才用两根手指从你手里接过缰绳。“嗯，”她说，“明天再来。”
# en: Ask Brask for help
opt.right.label [e6a413] = 请布拉斯克帮忙
# en: "I can't," you say. "Show me." Brask comes over from the fence, takes your hands and puts them on the rope the right way, and the griffin goes quiet as a cat. "Good," she says. "Most never ask." You realise she's remembering it.
opt.right.say.1 [b3a8df] = “我不行，”你说，“教教我。”布拉斯克从栅栏边走过来，把你的手按到缰绳上正确的位置，狮鹫一下子安静得像只猫。“很好，”她说，“大多数人从不开口。”你意识到，她会记住这一次。

@event heard_bram_corvin
# en: Bram on Corvin
title [577591] = 布拉姆谈科尔文
# en: Bram takes you aside, which he never does. "You're friendly with Corvin," he says, not quite a question. "Then you should know. He's on his last warning. One more detention and they send him home." He looks at the fountain, where Corvin is laughing at something. "I shouldn't have told you. I'm telling you anyway."
text [a93314] = 布拉姆把你拉到一边，他从不这么做。“你和科尔文走得近，”他说，不太像问句，“那你该知道。他在最后警告期。再挨一次禁闭，他们就送他回家。”他看着喷泉边正为什么事笑着的科尔文。“我不该告诉你的。可我还是告诉你了。”
# en: A courtyard at noon, a prefect in a red sash speaking low to a student, glancing across at another student lounging by the fountain.
scene [8e80b7] = 正午的庭院，一位系红绶带的级长压低声音对一个学生说话，瞥向喷泉边懒洋洋靠着的另一个学生。
# en: Thank Bram, and keep it quiet
opt.left.label [8ef4ba] = 谢谢布拉姆，保守秘密
# en: You thank him, and don't tell anyone. Over the next month you notice yourself steering Corvin away from trouble, without saying why. Bram notices too, and pretends not to.
opt.left.say.1 [15981d] = 你谢过他，没告诉任何人。接下来的一个月，你发现自己总在不动声色地把科尔文从麻烦边上引开。布拉姆也注意到了，假装没看见。
# en: Ask Bram why he cares
opt.right.label [662703] = 问布拉姆为什么在乎
# en: "Why do you care?" you ask. Bram goes red. "Somebody has to," he says, and walks off. You don't tell Corvin what Bram said. You do sit with him at lunch more, and he notices, and makes a joke of it.
opt.right.say.1 [429bbf] = “你为什么在乎？”你问。布拉姆脸红了。“总得有人在乎，”他说完就走了。你没告诉科尔文布拉姆说了什么。你倒是午饭时更常和他坐在一起了，他注意到了，还拿这事开玩笑。

@event heard_corvin_bram
# en: Corvin on Bram
title [22e611] = 科尔文谈布拉姆
# en: Corvin is shuffling his deck on the parapet. "You know why Bram's like he is?" he says. "His father was head boy. Tells him every holiday he'll never amount to anything. I heard it myself, on the stairs, one parents' day." He deals a card and looks at it. "Don't tell him I told you. He'd hate that more than anything I've ever done to him."
text [489be4] = 科尔文在矮墙上洗着牌。“你知道布拉姆为什么是那个样子吗？”他说，“他父亲当年是男生学生会主席。每个假期都告诉他，他不会有出息。我亲耳听到的，在楼梯上，有一年家长日。”他发了一张牌，看了看。“别告诉他是我说的。比起我对他做过的任何事，他会更恨这个。”
# en: A gargoyle passage at night, a student shuffling cards on a parapet, telling a story to another in a low voice.
scene [e88648] = 夜里的石像鬼通道，一个学生在矮墙上洗着牌，低声给另一个人讲一个故事。
# en: Keep it to yourself
opt.left.label [09de43] = 自己知道就好
# en: You keep it to yourself. But the next time Bram gives you a demerit, you hear his father's voice under it, and you take it a little more gently than before. Bram notices, and doesn't know why.
opt.left.say.1 [0d2cf8] = 你没告诉任何人。可下一次布拉姆给你记过时，你听见了藏在底下的他父亲的声音，你接受得比以前温和了一点。布拉姆注意到了，却不知道为什么。
# en: Ask Corvin why he told you
opt.right.label [996936] = 问科尔文为什么告诉你
# en: "Why tell me?" you ask. Corvin shuffles. "So someone's kind to him," he says, "and it isn't me." Then he deals you a hand, and talks about something else very fast.
opt.right.say.1 [9e0101] = “为什么告诉我？”你问。科尔文洗着牌。“好让有人对他好一点，”他说，“而那个人不是我。”然后他给你发了一手牌，飞快地聊起了别的事。

@event heard_maud_thorne
# en: Maud on Thorne
title [361335] = 莫德谈索恩
# en: Maud is cutting back the hedge. "You know old Thorne?" she says. "Every dawn, dearie, he's up behind the observatory in that little walled garden of his, talking to his roses. Thinks nobody knows. I've known for thirty years." She snips. "He's kinder to them than to any of you. Don't tell him I said."
text [f5c2b7] = 莫德在修剪树篱。“你认识老索恩吧？”她说，“每天黎明，亲爱的，他都在观星台后面那个围墙小花园里，跟他的玫瑰说话。以为没人知道。我知道三十年了。”她剪了一刀。“他对玫瑰比对你们谁都好。别告诉他是我说的。”
# en: A cottage garden at dusk, an old woman pruning a hedge with shears, nodding toward the dark shape of an observatory on the hill.
scene [7bbafe] = 黄昏时的小屋花园，一位老妇人拿着剪子修剪树篱，朝山上观星台黑黢黢的轮廓点了点头。
# en: Promise not to tell
opt.left.label [a46fa3] = 答应不说出去
# en: You promise. You don't tell. But the next time Thorne is terrible to you in a lecture, you imagine him at dawn, talking to a rose, and it helps more than you'd have thought.
opt.left.say.1 [eecd1a] = 你答应了。你没说出去。可下一次索恩在课上对你很凶时，你想象他在黎明跟一朵玫瑰说话，这比你想象的还管用。
# en: Ask whether she'd show you
opt.right.label [776870] = 问她能不能带你去看看
# en: "Show you? Certainly not," says Maud, delighted. She does anyway, from behind the hedge one dawn, both of you crouching. Thorne is pruning and murmuring. He looks up, just once, at the hedge. You both hold your breath.
opt.right.say.1 [05220e] = “带你去看？当然不行，”莫德说，乐坏了。可她还是带你去了，某个黎明，你们俩一起蹲在树篱后面。索恩一边修剪一边低语。他抬起头，只有一次，看向那道树篱。你们俩都屏住了呼吸。

@event heard_mabel_grimsby
# en: Mabel on Grimsby
title [b13f12] = 梅布尔谈格林斯比
# en: "Shut again," says Mabel, nodding at Grimsby's across the lane. "You know where he goes, petal? Lighthouses. Walks out to look at one, any one, whenever the shop gets too much. Forty years I've watched him go." She pours your tea. "He thinks it's a secret. Everyone in the village knows."
text [0bfe0d] = “又关门了，”梅布尔朝巷子对面的格林斯比书店点点头，“你知道他去哪儿吗，小可爱？灯塔。只要书店让他受不了，他就走出去看一座灯塔，随便哪一座。我看着他这么走了四十年。”她给你倒了茶。“他以为这是秘密。全村人都知道。”
# en: A village tea shop, a woman behind the counter wiping cups, nodding through the window at a bookshop across the lane with its sign turned to closed.
scene [f6be2b] = 村里的茶馆，一个女人在柜台后擦着杯子，隔着窗户朝巷子对面一家挂着打烊牌子的书店点了点头。
# en: Keep his secret, such as it is
opt.left.label [88b9ea] = 替他保守这个秘密
# en: You keep it, such as it is. Next time you're in the shop, you notice the little brass lighthouse on his counter for the first time, and the picture of one above the till, and you don't say anything.
opt.left.say.1 [6dda65] = 你替他守着这个秘密，如果它还算秘密的话。下次去书店时，你第一次注意到他柜台上那座小小的黄铜灯塔，还有收银台上方的一幅灯塔画，你什么也没说。
# en: Ask which lighthouse he likes best
opt.right.label [7a98fe] = 问他最喜欢哪座灯塔
# en: "The one at the point," says Mabel at once. "It's the ugliest. He says it tries the hardest." She thinks about it. "That's the nicest thing anyone's ever said about anything round here, and he said it about a lighthouse."
opt.right.say.1 [230c8e] = “岬角上那座，”梅布尔立刻说，“最丑的那座。他说它最努力。”她想了想。“这是这一带有人对任何东西说过的最好听的话，而他是对一座灯塔说的。”

@event heard_marisol_vey
# en: Marisol on Vey
title [020979] = 玛丽索尔谈维伊
# en: Marisol closes her book of poems. "Has Vey shown you the mirror trick yet?" she asks. "She won't, in public. Once, years ago, her reflection didn't come back for a week. Walked around the castle as her. Taught two of her classes." She looks at the rain. "Vey still won't talk about it. I think she was frightened. I think she still is."
text [8403ea] = 玛丽索尔合上了她的诗集。“维伊给你看过镜子把戏了吗？”她问，“她不会当众做的。很多年前有一次，她的倒影一个星期都没回来。顶着她的样子在城堡里走来走去。替她上了两节课。”她望着雨。“维伊到现在都不肯谈这件事。我想她是被吓到了。我想她现在还怕。”
# en: A rainy lakeshore, a professor reading under a dry patch of air on the steps, talking quietly to a student beside her.
scene [658626] = 下雨的湖岸，一位教授坐在台阶上一块干燥的空气下读书，低声对身边的学生说话。
# en: Promise never to mention it to Vey
opt.left.label [0901d9] = 答应永远不对维伊提起
# en: You promise. You never mention it. But the next time Vey passes the long mirror on the stairs, you see her glance at it, just once, and look away quickly, and you understand.
opt.left.say.1 [8b182a] = 你答应了。你从没提起过。可下一次维伊经过楼梯上那面长镜时，你看见她朝镜子瞥了一眼，就一眼，又飞快地移开了目光，你明白了。
# en: Ask who noticed it wasn't her
opt.right.label [2a9b3c] = 问是谁发现那不是她
# en: "Nobody," says Marisol. "That's what frightened her. Nobody noticed for a week." She opens her book again. "The poem I can't remember the end of is about that. I've just realised."
opt.right.say.1 [c13193] = “没人发现，”玛丽索尔说，“这才是吓到她的地方。一个星期都没人发现。”她又翻开了书。“我总记不起结尾的那首诗，写的就是这件事。我刚刚才意识到。”

@event heard_nessa_isolde
# en: Nessa on the Headmistress
title [7697af] = 内莎谈院长
# en: Nessa taps a sketch on her wall: the headmistress's tower, one window circled. "Tower chess," she says. "Every evening. She plays both sides, and when she loses to herself she laughs out loud. I've heard it from the courtyard." She lowers her voice. "That's my way in, one day. Nobody interviews a woman who's winning."
text [b177f5] = 内莎敲了敲墙上的一张速写：院长塔，一扇窗户被圈了出来。“塔棋，”她说，“每天晚上。她自己跟自己下，输给自己时会大笑出声。我在庭院里都听见过。”她压低声音。“那就是我的突破口，总有一天。没人能采访一个正在赢棋的女人。”
# en: A newspaper office, an editor pointing at a sketch of a tower window pinned to a cluttered wall, a student leaning in to look.
scene [6f4e93] = 报社办公室里，一位编辑指着钉在杂乱墙上的一张塔窗速写，一个学生凑过去看。
# en: Wish her luck with the interview
opt.left.label [3ad1a6] = 祝她采访顺利
# en: You wish her luck. She says she doesn't need luck, she needs a chessboard, and spends the evening learning tower chess from a library book with a great deal of muttering. She's terrible at it.
opt.left.say.1 [857f68] = 你祝她好运。她说她不需要运气，她需要一副棋盘，然后花了一个晚上，嘟嘟囔囔地对着图书馆的一本书学塔棋。她下得糟透了。
# en: Ask her not to use it as a trick
opt.right.label [87a971] = 请她别拿这个当把戏
# en: "Don't make it a trick," you say. Nessa looks at you for a long moment. "It isn't a trick," she says. "It's a door." But she takes the sketch down off the wall, and puts it in a drawer.
opt.right.say.1 [737eab] = “别把它当成把戏，”你说。内莎看了你好一会儿。“这不是把戏，”她说，“这是一扇门。”可她还是把那张速写从墙上取下来，放进了抽屉。

@event heard_tobias_mir
# en: Tobias on Mir
title [86c9da] = 托拜厄斯谈米尔
# en: "Mir's family," Tobias says, repotting, "run a clockworks. Big one. And they think all of it, the inventing, is a hobby." He presses the soil down very gently. "Mir told me that like it was nothing. It wasn't nothing. On the farm we'd say a calf that isn't let run never learns its legs."
text [859f7b] = “米尔家，”托拜厄斯一边换盆一边说，“开着一间钟表工坊。很大的一间。他们觉得那些东西，那些发明，全都只是爱好。”他非常轻地压实泥土。“米尔跟我说的时候，就像那不算什么。那可不是不算什么。在农场上我们说，不让跑的小牛犊永远学不会用腿。”
# en: A greenhouse in the afternoon, a broad farm boy repotting seedlings and talking over his shoulder to a student holding a watering can.
scene [24d787] = 午后的温室里，一个壮实的农家男孩一边给秧苗换盆，一边回头对一个拿着水壶的学生说话。
# en: Say you'll keep it between you
opt.left.label [a94b5d] = 说这话就你们俩知道
# en: "Between us," you say. Tobias nods, relieved. Later you notice that every time someone calls one of Mir's machines "a nice little toy", Tobias, very politely, changes the subject.
opt.left.say.1 [59db45] = “就我们俩知道，”你说。托拜厄斯松了口气，点点头。后来你注意到，每当有人管米尔的机器叫“不错的小玩具”，托拜厄斯都会非常客气地岔开话题。
# en: Say Mir should hear that saying
opt.right.label [e5e097] = 说米尔该听听这句老话
# en: "Tell Mir that," you say. Tobias goes pink. He does, a week later, at supper, and gets it slightly wrong, and Mir laughs, and then goes quiet, and then says it back to him, correctly, as if writing it down.
opt.right.say.1 [89d853] = “把这句话告诉米尔，”你说。托拜厄斯脸红了。一个星期后，他在晚饭时说了，说得有点不对，米尔笑了，然后安静下来，然后把这句话一字不差地说给他听，就像在把它记下来。

@event heard_grimsby_mabel
# en: Grimsby on Mabel
title [e5cb12] = 格林斯比谈梅布尔
# en: Grimsby nods across the lane at Mabel's. "Those cups behind her counter," he says. "Every one belongs to a regular. Living or dead. She never takes one down." He turns a page without reading it. "Mine's the blue one, third from the left. She hung it my first winter in the village, when I knew nobody. I've never told her I know why."
text [f20660] = 格林斯比朝巷子对面的梅布尔茶馆点点头。“她柜台后面那些杯子，”他说，“每一只都属于一位常客。活着的，还是去世的。她从不取下任何一只。”他翻过一页，并没在读。“我的是蓝色那只，左数第三个。她是在我刚来村里的第一个冬天挂上的，那时我谁也不认识。我从没告诉过她，我知道为什么。”
# en: A bookshop window, an old bookseller pointing across the lane at a tea shop with cups hanging on hooks behind its counter.
scene [db4641] = 书店的橱窗前，一位老书商指着巷子对面一家茶馆，茶馆柜台后面的挂钩上挂着一排杯子。
# en: Keep it between you and him
opt.left.label [6096ed] = 这事就你们俩知道
# en: You keep it. The next time you're at Mabel's, you look for the blue cup, third from the left, and find it, and say nothing. Mabel sees you looking, and smiles, and pours your tea.
opt.left.say.1 [674eb1] = 你守住了这件事。下次去梅布尔那里，你寻找那只蓝杯子，左数第三个，找到了，什么也没说。梅布尔看见你在看，笑了笑，给你倒了茶。
# en: Ask whether he'll tell her
opt.right.label [884e69] = 问他会不会告诉她
# en: "Will you tell her?" you ask. Grimsby considers it, then shakes his head. "She knows I know," he says. "That's the whole arrangement." He sells you a book about lighthouses you didn't ask for. You buy it.
opt.right.say.1 [69fdcb] = “你会告诉她吗？”你问。格林斯比想了想，摇了摇头。“她知道我知道，”他说，“这就是全部的默契。”他卖给你一本你没要的关于灯塔的书。你买了。

@event sell_a_secret
# en: What's It Worth?
title [cebc57] = 值多少钱？
# en: The man who prints the gossip sheets in the village stops you in the lane. He's heard you're close to {x}, he says, and that you know something about {x.them} nobody else does. "Whatever it is," he says, weighing a purse, "from someone like you, it would sell out by noon. Your name on it, if you like. Or not."
text [78d642] = 村里印八卦小报的那个人在巷子里拦住你。他说他听说你和{x}很要好，还知道一件关于{x.them}的、别人都不知道的事。“不管是什么，”他掂着一只钱袋说，“从你这样的人嘴里说出来，不到中午就能卖光。愿意的话，署你的名。不愿意也行。”
# en: A village lane, a sly man in a printer's apron leaning in a doorway, holding up a purse, a student stopped in front of him.
scene [ffc4ee] = 村里的一条小巷，一个系着印刷工围裙、神情狡黠的男人倚在门口，举着一只钱袋，一个学生在他面前停下脚步。
# en: Sell it
opt.left.label [4ac442] = 卖了
# en: You tell him. The sheet sells out by noon. {x} comes to breakfast, reads it, puts down {x.their} fork, and looks across the hall at you, and doesn't say anything at all. That's the worst part.
opt.left.say.1 [75c754] = 你告诉了他。小报不到中午就卖光了。{x}来吃早饭，读了它，放下{x.their}叉子，隔着大厅看着你，一句话也没说。这才是最难受的。
# en: Say you know nothing
opt.right.label [b227c3] = 说你什么都不知道
# en: "Never heard of it," you say, and walk on. The man shrugs and pockets his purse. That evening {x} sits down beside you at supper for no reason {x.they} could name, and stays longer than usual.
opt.right.say.1 [89630a] = “没听说过，”你说完就走了。那人耸耸肩，收起了钱袋。那天晚上，{x}在晚饭时坐到你身边，{x.they}自己也说不出为什么，而且比平时待得久。

@event scandal_secret_out
# en: Who Sold It
title [d89340] = 是谁卖的
# en: It's out: everyone knows who sold the gossip sheet the story about {npc}. The printer told the Newt, and the Newt told the castle. People who never cared for {npc} are disgusted with you anyway: nobody likes someone who sells a friend. {npc} hasn't said a word. Everyone is waiting to see what you'll do.
text [17c57f] = 事情败露了：所有人都知道是谁把{npc}的事卖给了八卦小报。印刷工告诉了蝾螈酒馆，蝾螈酒馆告诉了城堡。那些从不在乎{npc}的人照样厌恶你：没人喜欢出卖朋友的人。{npc}一个字都没说。大家都在等你怎么做。
# en: A refectory at breakfast, a gossip sheet passed hand to hand, a whole table turning to look at one student, another student sitting very straight at the next table.
scene [26df37] = 早餐时的膳堂，一份八卦小报在人们手里传着，一整张桌子的人转头看向一个学生，另一张桌子边一个学生坐得笔直。
# en: Apologise to {npc}, in front of everyone
opt.own.label [da654c] = 当着所有人的面向{npc}道歉
# en: You stand up at breakfast, cross the hall and apologise to {npc}, out loud, with everyone watching. {They} look{s} at you for a long time, and then nod{s}, once. It doesn't mend it. It's a start.
opt.own.say.1 [f17247] = 早饭时你站起来，穿过大厅，当着所有人的面大声向{npc}道歉。{they}看了你很久，然后点了一下头。这并没有弥补什么。但这是个开始。
# en: Say the printer is lying
opt.deny.label [e40b0c] = 说印刷工在撒谎
# en: You say the printer is a liar who'd sell his own mother, which is true. People decide to believe you, more or less. {npc} doesn't, and says nothing, and doesn't need to.
opt.deny.say.1 [6d356b] = 你说那个印刷工是个连亲娘都肯卖的骗子，这倒是真的。人们大体上决定相信你。{npc}不信，却什么也没说，也用不着说。
# en: You say the printer is lying, and the printer produces the receipt with your initial on it. The castle has its verdict. {npc} walks past you in the corridor as if you were a draught.
opt.deny.say.2 [3f2a1f] = 你说印刷工在撒谎，印刷工拿出了收据，上面有你名字的首字母。城堡有了定论。{npc}在走廊里从你身边走过，就像你是一阵穿堂风。
# en: Say it was true, and someone had to
opt.spin.label [8e107d] = 说那是真的，总得有人说
# en: You say, coolly, that it was true, and someone had to say it. Some people agree with you. {npc} hears it. {They} stop{s} coming to meals for a week, and the castle forgets who started it, and you never will.
opt.spin.say.1 [e1bce9] = 你冷冷地说，那是真的，总得有人说出来。有些人同意你。{npc}听到了。{they}一个星期没来吃饭，城堡忘了是谁起的头，而你永远不会忘。
